<%# The topless-rise sweep's pre-registered reading (docs/design_record.md, 2026-10-02,
    "Topless rise: does the deepest rung held keep rising when depth is paid?"): `reading` is a
    Lab::ToplessRiseReading::Report. The per-child rows stay in `lab:topless_rise_report`. %>
<section class="mt-6" id="topless-rise-reading">
  <h2>
    The pre-registered reading
    <% if reading.any? %>
      <span class="badge <%= reading.interim? ? 'badge-warning' : 'badge-success' %>">
        <%= reading.interim? ? "interim" : "final" %>
      </span>
    <% end %>
    <%= render "findings/objective_badge" %>
  </h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted">
    <% if reading.interim? %>
      Interim: not every child of every qualifying parent has finished, and nothing here is the
      sweep's result yet.
    <% else %>
      Every child of every qualifying parent has finished.
    <% end %>
    Each child continues a world of the
    <%= link_to "Meta-stack", experiment_path(Lab::ToplessRiseReading::PARENTS.fetch("experiment")) %> sweep
    and is paired with the child of the same parent in another arm. All are read over their own
    samples past a settling window of
    <%= number_with_delimiter Lab::ToplessRiseReading::SETTLING_WINDOW %> epochs. A child rises late
    where the median depth of the deepest rung held by a tenth of the world, over the last tenth of
    those samples, is at least <%= Lab::ToplessRiseReading::RISE_STEP %> above its median over the
    fifth tenth. A child already at depth <%= Lab::ToplessRiseReading::CEILING_DEPTH %>, the deepest a
    reading can show, by its fifth tenth is ceilinged and read as no rise. A child is extinct where
    its last-decile median share of replicators is below
    <%= percent_value Lab::ToplessRiseReading::EXTINCT_SHARE %>, and a pair with an extinct child is in
    no test. Each test is a one-sided sign test at p &lt; <%= Lab::ToplessRiseReading::SIGN_TEST_LEVEL %>,
    re-read with the extinct pairs kept and on the children of Meta-stack's nine deep children alone.
    This substrate imports an objective, a primitive, a hereditary channel, the primitive's
    semantics and a ladder of growing input arity, so rung 4 on Soup stays not shown whatever it
    reads.
  </p>

  <% if reading.any? %>
    <figure class="table-figure mt-4">
      <figcaption class="table-caption text-sm text-muted" id="topless-rise-arms">
        Children per arm, read so far. Measured means read on both tenths and not extinct; reached
        the floor means depth <%= Lab::ToplessRiseReading::CEILING_DEPTH %>, "13 or more", in any sample.
      </figcaption>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="topless-rise-arms">
        <table class="data-table" aria-labelledby="topless-rise-arms">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Arm</th>
              <th class="numeric">Children</th>
              <th class="numeric">Finished</th>
              <th class="numeric">Settled relapses</th>
              <th class="numeric">Extinct</th>
              <th class="numeric">Measured</th>
              <th class="numeric">Rise late</th>
              <th class="numeric">Ceilinged</th>
              <th class="numeric">Reached the floor</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% reading.arms.each do |arm| %>
              <tr>
                <td><%= arm.name %></td>
                <% arm.cells.drop(1).each do |count| %>
                  <td class="numeric"><%= count %></td>
                <% end %>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </figure>

    <% if reading.mostly_ceilinged? %>
      <p class="alert alert-warning mt-4" id="topless-rise-near-top">
        Most of the rise arm's children are ceilinged: the ladder had a near top after all, and
        the tests below are not read as an answer.
      </p>
    <% end %>

    <h3 class="mt-4">Hypotheses</h3>
    <ul>
      <% reading.readings.each do |test, kept, deep| %>
        <% comparison = test.comparison %>
        <li class="mb-3">
          <strong><%= test.hypothesis %></strong>, <%= test.treatment.name %> against <%= test.control.name %>:
          <span class="badge <%= test.badge_class %>"><%= test.outcome_label %></span>
          <p class="text-sm text-muted">
            <%= pluralize(comparison.measured_count, "pair") %> measured on both sides:
            <%= comparison.favouring %> favour <%= test.treatment.name %>, <%= comparison.against %>
            <%= test.control.name %>,
            <%= comparison.ties %> tie<% if comparison.p_value %>; p = <%= p_value_text comparison.p_value %><% end %>.
            <% if comparison.carried_by.any? %>
              Carried by parents
              <%= comparison.carried_by.map { |parents| parents.map { |id| "run #{id}" }.join(" and ") }.to_sentence(two_words_connector: " or ", last_word_connector: ", or ") %>:
              without their pairs the test falls to p ≥ <%= Lab::ToplessRiseReading::SIGN_TEST_LEVEL %>.
            <% end %>
            <% [["With the extinct pairs kept", kept], ["On the deep parents' children", deep]].each do |label, other| %>
              <%= label %>:
              <span class="badge <%= other.badge_class %>"><%= other.outcome_label %></span>,
              <%= other.comparison.favouring %> to <%= other.comparison.against %><% if other.comparison.p_value %>,
              p = <%= p_value_text other.comparison.p_value %><% end %>.
            <% end %>
          </p>
          <% if comparison.agreement.any? %>
            <details class="text-sm">
              <summary>Per-parent agreement</summary>
              <table class="data-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Parent</th>
                    <th class="numeric">Favour <%= test.treatment.name %></th>
                    <th class="numeric">Favour <%= test.control.name %></th>
                    <th class="numeric">Tie</th>
                    <th class="numeric">Not both measured</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <% comparison.agreement.each do |row| %>
                    <tr>
                      <td><%= link_to "run #{row.parent_id}", run_path(row.parent_id) %></td>
                      <td class="numeric"><%= row.treatment %></td>
                      <td class="numeric"><%= row.continuation %></td>
                      <td class="numeric"><%= row.ties %></td>
                      <td class="numeric"><%= row.unmeasured %></td>
                    </tr>
                  <% end %>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </details>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>

    <% if reading.ceilinged.any? %>
      <p class="text-sm mt-4" id="topless-rise-ceilinged">
        Ceilinged, read as no rise:
        <%= safe_join(reading.ceilinged.map { |child| link_to("run #{child.run_id} (#{child.treatment.name})", run_path(child.run_id)) }, ", ") %>.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <p class="mt-4">No child yet.</p>
  <% end %>
</section>
